{
  "_help": {
    "_file": "The 7 AI personalities: WHAT each one wants. (How well it plays is the skill — skills.json.) Starting values from the original game's festive-booth AI (research/original-digest.md §2); the Personality Check (feel-targets.json) tunes them. Notes are keyed by the setting's name inside ONE personality, so they fit every personality in the list.",
    "id": "The personality's name in code. Its name and bio for players live in content/text/en.json → ai.personality.<id>.",
    "traits": "Seven traits, each a range 0–100. Every turn it picks a value inside each range, so it leans the same way but never plays exactly alike twice. A higher trait = its goal wins the goal roll more often.",
    "traits.aggression": "TRAP — hem rival glyphlings in, cut their moves, tangle them, take territory.",
    "traits.greed": "SCORE — make the most Magic this turn.",
    "traits.spite": "DENY — block a rival's lines and near-words; toss a weed where a rival would score.",
    "traits.caution": "ESCAPE — keep its own glyphlings roomy and safe; keep pockets only it can reach.",
    "traits.patience": "BUILD — set up its own future words (gaps, extensions, crossings).",
    "traits.opportunism": "STEAL — grow a rival's word into one it owns most of.",
    "traits.pragmatism": "DUMP — shed junk letters, far from every glyphling.",
    "goals": "The goal roll walks this list in order: each goal rolls against its trait; the first to succeed is the turn's main goal (all fail → the first one).",
    "nudge": "0–1. How much the OTHER goals count when scoring a move. 0 = only the main goal (the original AI); higher = it favours two-birds moves.",
    "shifts": "Mood shifts: when a reading (0–10) climbs from `from` to `full`, the trait's whole range moves by up to `by`. `from` above `full` = it grows as the reading FALLS. Readings: myDanger, rivalDanger, fill (board fill), behind / ahead (believed Magic gap), handQuality (10 = great), territory, endNear.",
    "chattiness": "0–100: how likely it is to say something at a banter moment (big moments only).",
    "extras.nerve": "How far ahead (in believed Magic) it must think it is before it ends the game itself (\"calls it\"). Lower = bolder, calls it wrong more often.",
    "extras.vocabulary": "Added to the skill's vocabulary threshold (Zipf). Negative = knows MORE words; positive = fewer.",
    "extras.extraWordBonus": "SCORE goal: bonus per extra word made in one cast (the original: 3). The Strategist — the two-words-one-move specialist — gets more."
  },
  "_labels": {
    "id": "Name (code)",
